The O1 design is in the plan, committed as 8f952ee and not pushed. The design defines:
- three dials: lights-on, hold and dark, one per stage, each lights-on until someone lowers it;
- which step each checkpoint folds into;
- merge as a real step;
- how old jobs and old settings map onto the new dials;
- the three assumptions I listed above, which you can overturn.

The build is next, and it is the largest change since P. It rewrites the core's `step` function, the dials, both pipelines, the store's reading of old jobs, the factory and Settings. Many core tests must change with it.

This session is long, and your session-hygiene rule says to compact after about 45 minutes of work. I suggest that you run `/compact` now, and I will start O1 in the core right after it. If you prefer to go on without compacting, say so and I will start now.

