Bastion = commercial multi-tenant cloud AI-governance platform (the paid cloud
version of `~/tacoda/open-refinery`, which is single-tenant/VPS). Built in
numbered phases tracked in `PLAN.md`; each phase gets its own stacked branch off
`main` (phase-0 → 1 → 2 → 2b → 3 → 6a-thin-ui …), committed but left unmerged.

**User wants to exercise changes in the browser as they're implemented** — not
just tests. Standing dev loop:
- API + postgres + redis run in Docker (`make up`); ports web 5173, api 8000,
  pg 5432, redis 6379.
- Frontend runs **locally via `bun run dev`** (Vite hot reload) — stop the
  `web` container first to free 5173. Faster than rebuilding the image per edit.
- `make test` = unit/api (no DB); `make test-int` = integration (needs pg+redis,
  migrations applied via `uv run alembic upgrade head`).

Stack: FastAPI + LangGraph (uv), React+Vite+TS+Tailwind v4 (bun), Postgres
(shared-DB + RLS multi-tenancy), Redis (Celery + sessions + device grants),
ports-and-adapters. Styling rule: Tailwind **semantic @apply classes**, never
inline utility soup; shadcn allowed but wrapped. See [[bastion-conventions]].
async fn request(target: &Server, to: &To<'_>) -> Result<Response, JsValue> {
    let headers = Headers::new()?;
    headers.set("Authorization", &format!("Bearer {}", target.token))?;
    if let Some(id) = to.last_event {
        headers.set("Last-Event-ID", id)?;
    }
    let init = RequestInit::new();
    init.set_method(to.method);
    if let Some(body) = to.body {
        headers.set("Content-Type", "application/json")?;
        init.set_body(&JsValue::from_str(&body.to_string()));
    }
    init.set_headers(&headers);
    let url = format!("{}{}", target.url.trim_end_matches('/'), to.path);
    let request = Request::new_with_str_and_init(&url, &init)?;
    let window = web_sys::window().ok_or("no window")?;
    Ok(JsFuture::from(window.fetch_with_request(&request))
        .await?
        .unchecked_into())
}

